# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type }})

Omit `instance_name` to create an organization-scoped API key v2. The organization must have AuthV2 enabled, and the provider's credentials must have permission to read the Organization. The provider checks these prerequisites before creating the key.

When `instance_name` is supplied, the server selects the API key version based on that instance's configuration. Existing configurations retain this behavior.

Changing or removing `instance_name` replaces the API key. To rotate an existing key, create a separate v2 resource and update clients before retiring the old key. Target clusters must support API key v2 before clients can use the new token.

## Example Usage

```terraform
resource "streamnative_apikey" "application" {
  organization         = "o-example"
  name                 = "application-key"
  service_account_name = "application"
  expiration_time      = "30d"
}
```

